From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 17:43:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: the elastic-reservation policy, pp_elastic.h

Decision 0180's rule as one pure header, with no Wine or Mach
dependency: whether an ask engages it, short grants, lending (the lender
and what it keeps), growth and refusal of a commit, and which view a
commit belongs to. Nothing changes until a placement fails; then the
large plain reservation with the most lendable room keeps
max(2h, h + 64 MiB) plus a 32 MiB guard and lends the rest, and an
unhinted reserve-only ask from 1 GiB to twice the guest window that
cannot be placed whole gets half the largest gap outside every live
claim, less the guard, at the gap's top and below earlier claims (for
The Witcher 3's first-match dispatch). A commit reaching
the guard grows its view by doubling while the space above is free,
else is refused with what blocked growth; it is matched to its own view
first, then to the covering claim, and never served in another view.
Hinted, aligned, placeholder, address-limited, commit-at-reserve and
Social Club layout asks are never shrunk, and so is a
WoW64 process's 4 GiB address window (PPE_ASK_WOW64, PLA-839): FEX
zero-extends a guest pointer over all of it. It is never tracked, so it
never lends; like any never-shrunk ask it can be lent room.

Lending and short grants come only from ppe_failed, after today's
placement failed: ppe_before answers PPE_PLACE (outside every live
claim) or PPE_TODAY. An ask carries its limit and alignment as named
fields (struct ppe_ask), and a never-shrunk ask is lent room only by a
lender whose freed range holds it there. A short grant is made only
while the view table has room for it. The state counts live claims.

The header returns decisions; the Wine glue (PLA-802) performs the
mappings, and its comment says how the glue calls it. Nothing calls it
yet. tools/tests/test_elastic_reserve.py compiles it as shipped here and
replays phone traces of Mewgenics, The Witcher 3 4.x and 1.32, RDR2 on
and off the Social Club layout, Hollow Knight, Death's Door, Portal 2's
WoW64 window and PLA-326's on a map without the increased-memory-limit
entitlement through it (tools/tests/fixtures/elastic/).

Linear: PLA-801, PLA-839
Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-11-02-elastic-reservations.md
Offered-upstream: no; the address-space layout is the iOS port's
---
 build/ntdll-unix/pp_elastic.h | 551 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 551 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 build/ntdll-unix/pp_elastic.h

diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/pp_elastic.h b/build/ntdll-unix/pp_elastic.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c5225db
--- /dev/null
+++ b/build/ntdll-unix/pp_elastic.h
@@ -0,0 +1,551 @@
+/* SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-or-later
+ * Elastic reservations (Playport, PLA-799, decision 0180): the policy.
+ *
+ * The guest gets about 47 GB of usable window and the Madeira layer backs
+ * every MEM_RESERVE with a host mapping of its full size, so games that
+ * reserve far more than they commit (Mewgenics' 1 GiB pools, The Witcher 3
+ * 4.x's 16/64/32 GiB pools) fill it, and the next reservation fails. This
+ * header holds every decision of the elastic rule; it maps nothing. The Wine
+ * glue (virtual_ios.c) performs the mappings it decides and reports back.
+ *
+ * Nothing changes until a placement fails. Then:
+ *  - lending: the lender with the most lendable room (an unhinted reserve-only
+ *    view of 256 MiB or more, not held, not committed to its top) keeps
+ *    max(2h, h + 64 MiB) plus a 32 MiB guard, h its committed height, and
+ *    gives the rest of its view back; its claim (the size the guest was told)
+ *    is remembered;
+ *  - short grants: an unhinted reserve-only ask from 1 GiB to twice the guest
+ *    window that cannot be placed whole gets half the largest free gap
+ *    outside every live claim, minus the guard, rounded down to 64 KiB, at
+ *    least 64 MiB, at the gap's top, below the lowest earlier claim when a gap
+ *    there allows; else after lending, in the room lending freed. The caller
+ *    is told it got its full size;
+ *  - growth: a commit reaching the guard or the claim beyond it grows the view
+ *    in place by doubling while the space above is free; otherwise it is
+ *    refused (STATUS_NO_MEMORY) with what blocked growth. A commit is matched
+ *    to the view that owns it first, then to the claim covering it; it is
+ *    never served in another view.
+ * Never shrunk, by property: hinted, aligned, placeholder, ...Ex with address
+ * requirements, zero_bits/limited and commit-at-reserve asks, and a WoW64
+ * process's address window.
+ * Asks the Social Club layout's router decides (any reserve passing its
+ * guards: layout held, verified helper) carry PPE_ASK_LAYOUT and get no
+ * decision here.
+ *
+ * "Live claims" are the promised extents of shortened views (short grants
+ * and lent views), [base, base + claim); a view still whole has none beyond
+ * itself.
+ *
+ * How the glue calls it (PLA-802), under virtual_mutex, one ppe_state per
+ * address space (the pseudo-processes share one):
+ *
+ *   reserve (after the Social Club router; ask: size, property flags and the
+ *   named limit and alignment it must meet):
+ *     d = ppe_before( st, &ask, gaps, n );   (PPE_TODAY or PPE_PLACE only)
+ *     if (d.kind == PPE_TODAY) { place as today; on success
+ *         ppe_placed( st, base, size, size, flags ); done; on STATUS_NO_MEMORY
+ *         d = ppe_failed( st, &ask, gaps, n ); }
+ *     loop on d.kind:
+ *       PPE_PLACE: map size bytes at d.addr (fixed, no-overwrite);
+ *                  ppe_placed( st, d.addr, size, size, flags ); done.
+ *       PPE_SHORT: map d.real + PPE_GUARD at d.addr, the guard PROT_NONE and
+ *                  never committable; mark the view elastic; report size;
+ *                  ppe_placed( st, d.addr, size, d.real, flags ); done.
+ *       PPE_LEND:  shrink view d.view to d.keep bytes (its last PPE_GUARD
+ *                  PROT_NONE), release the rest to the host;
+ *                  ppe_lent( st, d.view, d.keep ); a never-shrunk ask then
+ *                  retries today's placement once and fails if that fails
+ *                  (the lender was picked for a freed range that can hold
+ *                  it); an elastic one asks ppe_failed( st, &ask, gaps, n )
+ *                  again.
+ *       PPE_FAIL:  return STATUS_NO_MEMORY as today.
+ *     gaps: the free ranges the ask may use (the guest window below FEX's
+ *     band, holds excluded), ascending, 64 KiB-aligned, re-read after a lend.
+ *   commit of [addr, addr + size):
+ *     i = ppe_owner( st, addr, base of the Wine view holding addr or 0 );
+ *     i < 0: not elastic, served as today (another view's own commit);
+ *     else c = ppe_commit( st, i, addr, size, free bytes from
+ *         ppe_view_end( st, i ) up, and the address that ends them );
+ *       PPE_SERVE: serve; ppe_served( st, i, addr, size ).
+ *       PPE_GROW:  map [ppe_view_end, + c.real - real) fixed no-overwrite,
+ *                  open the old guard; ppe_grown( st, i, c.real ); serve and
+ *                  ppe_served.
+ *       PPE_REFUSE: STATUS_NO_MEMORY, logged with c.blocker.
+ *   release of a view: ppe_released( st, base ).
+ *   a WoW64 process's window (PLA-839; Wine reserves it, the guest never
+ *   asks): ask { IOS_WOW64_WINDOW_SIZE, PPE_ASK_WOW64 }, placed as today
+ *   (its fixed slots, then a first fit; ppe_before has nothing for a
+ *   never-shrunk ask); when that fails, d = ppe_failed( st, &ask, gaps, n ):
+ *   a PPE_LEND as above, then today's placement once more; else it fails.
+ * Lend, grant, grow and refuse each log one tagged line with the address,
+ * real size, claim and committed height.
+ *
+ * Pure, so a host test (tools/tests/test_elastic_reserve.py) compiles this
+ * header as is and replays phone traces through it. */
+#ifndef PP_ELASTIC_H
+#define PP_ELASTIC_H
+#include <stdint.h>
+
+#define PPE_GRAIN       UINT64_C(0x10000)        /* allocation granularity */
+#define PPE_GUARD       (UINT64_C(32) << 20)     /* PROT_NONE above a shortened view */
+#define PPE_LENDER_MIN  (UINT64_C(256) << 20)    /* smallest view that lends */
+#define PPE_SHORT_MIN   (UINT64_C(1) << 30)      /* smallest ask a short grant serves */
+#define PPE_SHORT_FLOOR (UINT64_C(64) << 20)     /* smallest real part of a short grant */
+#define PPE_KEEP_MARGIN (UINT64_C(64) << 20)     /* a lender keeps at least h + this */
+#define PPE_VIEWS_MAX   1024
+
+/* Properties of an ask. Any of PPE_ASK_WHOLE: never shrunk. */
+#define PPE_ASK_HINT        0x001u  /* a base address was given */
+#define PPE_ASK_ALIGN       0x002u  /* an alignment requirement */
+#define PPE_ASK_PLACEHOLDER 0x004u  /* MEM_RESERVE_PLACEHOLDER / MEM_REPLACE_PLACEHOLDER */
+#define PPE_ASK_EX_ADDR     0x008u  /* ...Ex with address requirements */
+#define PPE_ASK_LIMIT       0x010u  /* zero_bits or an upper limit */
+#define PPE_ASK_COMMIT      0x020u  /* MEM_COMMIT at reserve time */
+#define PPE_ASK_LAYOUT      0x040u  /* the Social Club layout's router decides it */
+#define PPE_ASK_WOW64       0x080u  /* a WoW64 process's address window */
+#define PPE_ASK_WHOLE       0x0ffu
+
+/* A WoW64 window is 4 GiB whatever the image: FEX zero-extends a 32-bit guest
+ * pointer to the window's base plus 32 bits, so every page of it is one the
+ * guest can name. Never shrunk is never tracked, so it never lends either:
+ * room given back from it would be guest addresses, and its commits go to the
+ * window's own allocator, never through ppe_served, so the policy could not
+ * know its committed height. */
+
+struct ppe_gap { uint64_t base, size; };
+
+/* An ask: its size, its property flags, and what a never-shrunk one requires
+ * of its place. */
+struct ppe_ask
+{
+    uint64_t size;
+    unsigned flags;   /* PPE_ASK_* */
+    uint64_t limit;   /* the address its place must end at or below; 0: none */
+    uint64_t align;   /* the alignment its base needs; 0: the 64 KiB grain */
+};
+
+/* Which free room a search may use. */
+enum ppe_room { PPE_ROOM_ANY, PPE_ROOM_OUTSIDE_CLAIMS };
+
+struct ppe_view
+{
+    uint64_t base;
+    uint64_t real;    /* bytes of usable view at base */
+    uint64_t guard;   /* PROT_NONE bytes above real: PPE_GUARD once shortened, else 0 */
+    uint64_t claim;   /* bytes the guest was told it has */
+    uint64_t high;    /* committed height: end of the highest commit, from base */
+};
+
+struct ppe_state
+{
+    uint64_t window;          /* bytes of guest window: an ask above twice it fails */
+    unsigned n, engaged, lends, shorts, grows, refusals;
+    unsigned shortened;       /* tracked views with real < claim: live claims */
+    struct ppe_view v[PPE_VIEWS_MAX];
+};
+
+enum ppe_kind { PPE_TODAY, PPE_FAIL, PPE_PLACE, PPE_SHORT, PPE_LEND };
+
+struct ppe_decision
+{
+    enum ppe_kind kind;
+    uint64_t addr;    /* PPE_PLACE, PPE_SHORT: where */
+    uint64_t real;    /* PPE_SHORT: usable bytes (the guard follows) */
+    uint64_t keep;    /* PPE_LEND: bytes the lender keeps, its guard included */
+    int view;         /* PPE_LEND: the lender */
+};
+
+enum ppe_commit_kind { PPE_SERVE, PPE_GROW, PPE_REFUSE };
+
+struct ppe_commit_decision
+{
+    enum ppe_commit_kind kind;
+    uint64_t real;     /* PPE_GROW: the view's new usable size */
+    uint64_t blocker;  /* PPE_REFUSE: the first address growth could not take */
+};
+
+static inline uint64_t ppe_down( uint64_t x ) { return x & ~(PPE_GRAIN - 1); }
+static inline uint64_t ppe_up( uint64_t x ) { return (x + PPE_GRAIN - 1) & ~(PPE_GRAIN - 1); }
+
+static inline void ppe_init( struct ppe_state *st, uint64_t window )
+{
+    st->window = window;
+    st->n = st->engaged = st->lends = st->shorts = st->grows = st->refusals = st->shortened = 0;
+}
+
+static inline int ppe_shortened( const struct ppe_view *v ) { return v->real < v->claim; }
+
+/* Whether any live claim exists (a shortened view). */
+static inline int ppe_any_shortened( const struct ppe_state *st ) { return st->shortened != 0; }
+
+/* End of the view's host mapping (its guard included). */
+static inline uint64_t ppe_view_end( const struct ppe_state *st, int i )
+{
+    return st->v[i].base + st->v[i].real + st->v[i].guard;
+}
+
+/* An ask the rule may shorten: unhinted, reserve-only, no exception. */
+static inline int ppe_elastic_ask( unsigned flags ) { return !(flags & PPE_ASK_WHOLE); }
+
+/* Whether a placed view is the module's to track: elastic, and of a lender's
+ * size or shortened. */
+static inline int ppe_tracks( uint64_t claim, uint64_t real, unsigned flags )
+{
+    return ppe_elastic_ask( flags ) && (ppe_up( claim ) >= PPE_LENDER_MIN || real < claim);
+}
+
+/* Whether ppe_before engages for this ask: after a failed placement, an
+ * elastic ask of a lender's size that is not over twice the window. */
+static inline int ppe_before_engages( const struct ppe_state *st, const struct ppe_ask *ask )
+{
+    return st->engaged && ppe_elastic_ask( ask->flags ) && ask->size >= PPE_LENDER_MIN && ask->size <= 2 * st->window;
+}
+
+/* The smallest free gap the module can use for an ask: a whole fit needs the
+ * ask, a short grant twice its floor and guard. Smaller gaps can be left out. */
+static inline uint64_t ppe_gap_min( uint64_t size )
+{
+    uint64_t whole = ppe_up( size ), shortg = 2 * (PPE_SHORT_FLOOR + PPE_GUARD);
+
+    return size >= PPE_SHORT_MIN && whole > shortg ? shortg : whole;
+}
+
+/* Whether [b, e) holds the ask whole, at its alignment and under its limit. */
+static inline int ppe_range_holds( uint64_t b, uint64_t e, const struct ppe_ask *ask )
+{
+    uint64_t align = ask->align > PPE_GRAIN ? ask->align : PPE_GRAIN, a = (b + align - 1) & ~(align - 1);
+
+    if (ask->limit && e > ask->limit) e = ask->limit;
+    return a < e && e - a >= ppe_up( ask->size );
+}
+
+/* Bytes the lender keeps, its guard included, at committed height h. */
+static inline uint64_t ppe_keep( uint64_t high )
+{
+    uint64_t twice = 2 * high, margin = high + PPE_KEEP_MARGIN;
+
+    return ppe_up( twice > margin ? twice : margin ) + PPE_GUARD;
+}
+
+/* The lender with the most lendable room, -1 if none has `need` bytes to lend.
+ * With `holds`, only a lender whose freed range holds that ask whole. */
+static inline int ppe_lender( const struct ppe_state *st, uint64_t need, const struct ppe_ask *holds,
+                              uint64_t *keep )
+{
+    uint64_t best = 0;
+    unsigned i;
+    int pick = -1;
+
+    for (i = 0; i < st->n; i++)
+    {
+        const struct ppe_view *v = &st->v[i];
+        uint64_t span = v->real + v->guard, k = ppe_keep( v->high );
+
+        if (v->claim < PPE_LENDER_MIN || v->high >= v->real || k >= span) continue;
+        if (holds && !ppe_range_holds( v->base + k, v->base + span, holds )) continue;
+        if (span - k > best) { best = span - k; pick = (int)i; *keep = k; }
+    }
+    if (pick >= 0 && best < need) pick = -1;
+    return pick;
+}
+
+/* The lowest base among live claims, or ~0 when there is none. */
+static inline uint64_t ppe_lowest_claim( const struct ppe_state *st )
+{
+    uint64_t low = ~UINT64_C(0);
+    unsigned i;
+
+    for (i = 0; i < st->n; i++)
+        if (ppe_shortened( &st->v[i] ) && st->v[i].base < low) low = st->v[i].base;
+    return low;
+}
+
+/* The next part of [b, e) at or after b outside every live claim: returns 0
+ * when none is left, else sets [*pb, *pe). */
+static inline int ppe_piece( const struct ppe_state *st, uint64_t b, uint64_t e, uint64_t *pb, uint64_t *pe )
+{
+    unsigned i, moved = 1;
+
+    while (moved && b < e)
+    {
+        moved = 0;
+        for (i = 0; i < st->n; i++)
+        {
+            const struct ppe_view *v = &st->v[i];
+            if (ppe_shortened( v ) && b >= v->base && b < v->base + v->claim)
+            {
+                b = v->base + v->claim;
+                moved = 1;
+            }
+        }
+    }
+    if (b >= e) return 0;
+    *pb = b;
+    *pe = e;
+    for (i = 0; i < st->n; i++)
+    {
+        const struct ppe_view *v = &st->v[i];
+        if (ppe_shortened( v ) && v->base > b && v->base < *pe) *pe = v->base;
+    }
+    return 1;
+}
+
+/* The real size a short grant gets from a gap of `size` bytes, 0 if too small. */
+static inline uint64_t ppe_short_real( uint64_t gap, uint64_t ask )
+{
+    uint64_t real;
+
+    if (gap / 2 <= PPE_GUARD) return 0;
+    real = ppe_down( gap / 2 - PPE_GUARD );
+    if (real > ask) real = ask;
+    return real >= PPE_SHORT_FLOOR ? real : 0;
+}
+
+/* The lowest whole fit for `size` among the gaps, in the given room: 0 when none. */
+static inline uint64_t ppe_fit( const struct ppe_state *st, uint64_t size, const struct ppe_gap *gaps,
+                                unsigned n, enum ppe_room room )
+{
+    unsigned g;
+
+    for (g = 0; g < n; g++)
+    {
+        uint64_t b = ppe_up( gaps[g].base ), e = ppe_down( gaps[g].base + gaps[g].size ), pb, pe;
+
+        if (room == PPE_ROOM_ANY)
+        {
+            if (b < e && e - b >= size) return b;
+            continue;
+        }
+        while (ppe_piece( st, b, e, &pb, &pe ))
+        {
+            if (pe - pb >= size) return pb;
+            b = pe;
+        }
+    }
+    return 0;
+}
+
+/* The largest gap in the given room below `below` as [*gb, *ge): its size, 0 if none. */
+static inline uint64_t ppe_largest( const struct ppe_state *st, const struct ppe_gap *gaps, unsigned n,
+                                    enum ppe_room room, uint64_t below, uint64_t *gb, uint64_t *ge )
+{
+    uint64_t best = 0;
+    unsigned g;
+
+    for (g = 0; g < n; g++)
+    {
+        uint64_t b = ppe_up( gaps[g].base ), e = ppe_down( gaps[g].base + gaps[g].size ), pb, pe;
+
+        if (e > below) e = below;
+        if (room == PPE_ROOM_ANY)
+        {
+            if (b < e && e - b > best) { best = e - b; *gb = b; *ge = e; }
+            continue;
+        }
+        while (ppe_piece( st, b, e, &pb, &pe ))
+        {
+            if (pe - pb > best) { best = pe - pb; *gb = pb; *ge = pe; }
+            b = pe;
+        }
+    }
+    return best;
+}
+
+/* A short grant for `size` in the largest gap of the given room, top-down. */
+static inline int ppe_short_in( const struct ppe_state *st, uint64_t size, const struct ppe_gap *gaps,
+                                unsigned n, enum ppe_room room, uint64_t below, struct ppe_decision *d )
+{
+    uint64_t gb = 0, ge = 0, real = ppe_short_real( ppe_largest( st, gaps, n, room, below, &gb, &ge ), size );
+
+    if (!real) return 0;
+    d->kind = PPE_SHORT;
+    d->real = real;
+    d->addr = ppe_down( ge - real - PPE_GUARD );
+    return 1;
+}
+
+/* Today's placement of an ask failed (STATUS_NO_MEMORY): what to do next. */
+static inline struct ppe_decision ppe_failed( struct ppe_state *st, const struct ppe_ask *ask,
+                                              const struct ppe_gap *gaps, unsigned n )
+{
+    struct ppe_decision d = { PPE_FAIL, 0, 0, 0, -1 };
+    uint64_t keep = 0, size;
+    int shortable;
+
+    if (ask->flags & PPE_ASK_LAYOUT) return d;
+    st->engaged = 1;
+    if (!ask->size || ask->size > 2 * st->window) return d;
+    if (!ppe_elastic_ask( ask->flags ))
+    {
+        /* Never shrunk: lend room for today's placement to retry in, unless
+         * the ask's place is given (a hint) or a hold serves it, and only
+         * from a lender whose freed range holds the ask at its alignment and
+         * under its limit. */
+        if (!(ask->flags & PPE_ASK_HINT) && (d.view = ppe_lender( st, ask->size, ask, &keep )) >= 0)
+        {
+            d.kind = PPE_LEND;
+            d.keep = keep;
+        }
+        return d;
+    }
+    size = ppe_up( ask->size );
+    /* A short grant is tracked or not made: past PPE_VIEWS_MAX the ask fails as today. */
+    shortable = size >= PPE_SHORT_MIN && st->n < PPE_VIEWS_MAX;
+    if ((d.addr = ppe_fit( st, size, gaps, n, PPE_ROOM_OUTSIDE_CLAIMS ))) { d.kind = PPE_PLACE; return d; }
+    if (shortable && (ppe_short_in( st, size, gaps, n, PPE_ROOM_OUTSIDE_CLAIMS, ppe_lowest_claim( st ), &d )
+                      || ppe_short_in( st, size, gaps, n, PPE_ROOM_OUTSIDE_CLAIMS, ~UINT64_C(0), &d )))
+        return d;
+    if (st->lends)
+    {
+        /* After lending: the room it freed lies inside the lenders' claims. */
+        if ((d.addr = ppe_fit( st, size, gaps, n, PPE_ROOM_ANY ))) { d.kind = PPE_PLACE; return d; }
+        if (shortable && ppe_short_in( st, size, gaps, n, PPE_ROOM_ANY, ~UINT64_C(0), &d )) return d;
+    }
+    d.addr = 0;
+    if ((d.view = ppe_lender( st, shortable ? ppe_gap_min( size ) : size, 0, &keep )) >= 0)
+    {
+        d.kind = PPE_LEND;
+        d.keep = keep;
+    }
+    return d;
+}
+
+/* Before today's placement: PPE_TODAY, or PPE_PLACE and nothing else. Until a
+ * placement has failed, and for asks smaller than a lender or never shrunk,
+ * PPE_TODAY: placed exactly as today. Once engaged, an elastic ask of lender
+ * size is placed outside every live claim when a gap there holds it whole, so
+ * a later pool does not land inside an earlier claim while room elsewhere
+ * allows; else it is placed as today. It never lends or shortens: those come
+ * only from ppe_failed, after today's placement failed. */
+static inline struct ppe_decision ppe_before( struct ppe_state *st, const struct ppe_ask *ask,
+                                              const struct ppe_gap *gaps, unsigned n )
+{
+    struct ppe_decision d = { PPE_TODAY, 0, 0, 0, -1 };
+
+    if (ppe_before_engages( st, ask ) && (d.addr = ppe_fit( st, ppe_up( ask->size ), gaps, n, PPE_ROOM_OUTSIDE_CLAIMS )))
+        d.kind = PPE_PLACE;
+    return d;
+}
+
+/* A reservation was placed at base: real usable bytes of claim promised.
+ * Tracks elastic reservations of lender size and every short grant; returns
+ * the view or -1. */
+static inline int ppe_placed( struct ppe_state *st, uint64_t base, uint64_t claim, uint64_t real, unsigned flags )
+{
+    struct ppe_view *v;
+
+    if (real >= claim) real = ppe_up( claim );   /* placed whole */
+    claim = ppe_up( claim );
+    if (!ppe_tracks( claim, real, flags ) || st->n >= PPE_VIEWS_MAX) return -1;
+    v = &st->v[st->n];
+    v->base = base;
+    v->real = real < claim ? real : claim;
+    v->guard = real < claim ? PPE_GUARD : 0;
+    v->claim = claim;
+    v->high = 0;
+    if (real < claim)
+    {
+        st->shorts++;
+        st->shortened++;
+    }
+    return (int)st->n++;
+}
+
+/* The glue shrank view i to keep bytes, its guard the last PPE_GUARD. */
+static inline void ppe_lent( struct ppe_state *st, int i, uint64_t keep )
+{
+    if (!ppe_shortened( &st->v[i] )) st->shortened++;
+    st->v[i].real = keep - PPE_GUARD;
+    st->v[i].guard = PPE_GUARD;
+    st->lends++;
+}
+
+/* The guest released the reservation at base: its claim ends. */
+static inline void ppe_released( struct ppe_state *st, uint64_t base )
+{
+    unsigned i;
+
+    for (i = 0; i < st->n; i++)
+        if (st->v[i].base == base)
+        {
+            if (ppe_shortened( &st->v[i] )) st->shortened--;
+            st->v[i] = st->v[--st->n];
+            return;
+        }
+}
+
+/* Which elastic view a commit at addr belongs to: the view the glue found
+ * holding it (view_base, 0 when no view does) first; a commit in another,
+ * untracked view is that view's (-1). With no view there, the claim covering
+ * addr whose base is nearest below it: the pool whose cursor ran past its end. */
+static inline int ppe_owner( const struct ppe_state *st, uint64_t addr, uint64_t view_base )
+{
+    uint64_t best = 0;
+    unsigned i;
+    int pick = -1;
+
+    for (i = 0; i < st->n; i++)
+        if (view_base && st->v[i].base == view_base) return (int)i;
+    if (view_base) return -1;
+    for (i = 0; i < st->n; i++)
+    {
+        const struct ppe_view *v = &st->v[i];
+        if (addr >= v->base && addr - v->base < v->claim && (pick < 0 || v->base > best))
+        {
+            best = v->base;
+            pick = (int)i;
+        }
+    }
+    return pick;
+}
+
+/* A commit of [addr, addr + size) in view i. free_above: free bytes from
+ * ppe_view_end( st, i ) up; next_owner: where they end (what blocks growth). */
+static inline struct ppe_commit_decision ppe_commit( struct ppe_state *st, int i, uint64_t addr, uint64_t size,
+                                                     uint64_t free_above, uint64_t next_owner )
+{
+    struct ppe_commit_decision c = { PPE_SERVE, 0, 0 };
+    const struct ppe_view *v = &st->v[i];
+    uint64_t end = addr + (size ? size : 1), need, target;
+
+    if (end < addr || addr < v->base || end - v->base > v->claim)
+    {
+        c.kind = PPE_REFUSE;   /* wraps, or past the claim: never the view's */
+        c.blocker = v->base + v->claim;
+        st->refusals++;
+        return c;
+    }
+    if (end - v->base <= v->real) return c;
+    need = ppe_up( end - v->base );
+    for (target = v->real ? v->real : PPE_GRAIN; target < need; target *= 2) ;
+    if (target > v->claim) target = v->claim;
+    if (target - v->real > ppe_down( free_above )) target = v->real + ppe_down( free_above );
+    if (target >= need)
+    {
+        c.kind = PPE_GROW;
+        c.real = target;
+        return c;
+    }
+    c.kind = PPE_REFUSE;
+    c.blocker = next_owner;
+    st->refusals++;
+    return c;
+}
+
+/* The glue grew view i in place to real usable bytes, the guard above. */
+static inline void ppe_grown( struct ppe_state *st, int i, uint64_t real )
+{
+    if (ppe_shortened( &st->v[i] ) && real >= st->v[i].claim) st->shortened--;
+    st->v[i].real = real;
+    st->grows++;
+}
+
+/* A commit of [addr, addr + size) in view i was served. */
+static inline void ppe_served( struct ppe_state *st, int i, uint64_t addr, uint64_t size )
+{
+    uint64_t top = addr + size - st->v[i].base;
+
+    if (top > st->v[i].high) st->v[i].high = top;
+}
+
+#endif
